{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/284423": {
      "title": "Director for Student Conduct and Title IX Deputy Coordinator",
      "description": "Director for Student Conduct and Title IX Deputy Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director for Student Conduct and Title IX Deputy Coordinator Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Master's Degree Preferred Category Student Development Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech is seeking a Director for Student Conduct and Title IX Deputy Coordinator to lead the university’s efforts in fostering a safe, inclusive, and respectful campus environment. The Director for Student Conduct and Deputy Title IX Coordinator will support the University’s efforts to create a learning and working environment that upholds community standards and is free from sex-and gender-based discrimination and misconduct.  The Director for Student Conduct manages the conduct process and system in support of student development and growth, providing advice, counsel, and regular updates to SVP Student Affairs.  As the Title IX Deputy Coordinator, the role assists with and supports compliance with Title IX and related federal and state regulations, while also contributing to civil rights policy development, bias reporting, and resolution processes.  This position will interact in a mature and positive manner with the student body. In addition to managing the conduct case load, the person will coordinate the education, prevention, and response efforts for the campus. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Student Conduct Maintain and enforce the student behavioral code of conduct while developing new policies as needed. Assure proper dissemination of university policies and guidelines to students and campus stakeholders. Serve as the primary student conduct officer, managing the case load, conducting investigations and fact-finding, meetings, and outcome communication. Utilize and serve as the lead administrator for the Maxient Conduct Management software for all case management intake processes. Train, coordinate, and collaborate with other administrators assisting with conduct management in other areas such as residential policies and students enrolled online. Collaborate with Residence Life, Athletics, Academic Affairs, and other relevant offices to support and communicate conduct investigations, findings, and decisions. Title IX Serve as a Title IX Deputy Coordinator, providing support to the Coordinator of Title IX. Ensure university compliance with federal guidelines. Uphold the integrity and timeline of the investigation process as well as maintain records of reports and outcomes. Maintain updated contacts for appropriate community resources as well as university provided resources. Maintain accurate records of reports, investigations, and outcomes in accordance with federal recordkeeping requirements, in conjunction with the Title IX Coordinator. Oversee training and ongoing education surrounding the Title IX policy for both students and employees, in conjunction with the Title IX Coordinator. Facilitate training for investigators, advisors, hearing panel members, and decision-makers, in conjunction with the Title IX Coordinator. Clery Act and VAWA Collaboration Work in partnership with Campus Safety, Student Affairs, and Institutional Research to support compliance with the Clery Act and the Violence Against Women Act (VAWA). Assist with annual security reporting, education/prevention programming, and coordinated response efforts. Help ensure accurate classification and reporting of Clery-designated incidents. Education, Prevention & Outreach Oversee and/or coordinate educational programming for Title IX, and substance abuse (alcohol and drugs). Collaborate on awareness efforts that promote a culture of respect, consent, and inclusion. Create accessible materials and resources for students, faculty, and staff. Serve on the BIT/CARE team. Administrative Engage, collaborate and communicate with all appropriate campus entities. Attend division, department, committee, and other meetings associated with the position. Provide role-model leadership to faculty, staff, and students. Perform other duties as assigned by the SVP in support of the institution Required Qualifications Bachelor’s required, Master’s degree preferred Excellent organizational, time management, and collaboration skills Excellent written and verbal communication Possess and display professional interpersonal and human relations skills Ability to effectively manage conflicts, stress, and related issues involving students, faculty, and administrators Preferred Qualifications Experience designing and delivering training to diverse campus audiences Certification in Title IX coordination or investigations (e.g., ATIXA, NACUA) Experience utilizing Maxient software for reporting and case management Experience Minimum of two years of experience in Title IX and/or student conduct administration in a higher education setting Minimum of five years of successful experience in a related field Computer Skills: Word               Intermediate Excel               Intermediate Outlook           Advanced Maxient          Advanced preferred Working Conditions Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment and various campus locations.  Some evening and weekend hours may be necessary to support campus events and various activities. **Application materials must include a cover letter and resume. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/283595": {
      "title": "Area Coordinator",
      "description": "Area Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Area Coordinator Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Master's Degree Preferred Category Student Development Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech seeks qualified candidates for a position in Residence Life. The Area Coordinator (AC) position is a live-in, 12-month position in our Residence Life Department. The Area Coordinator plays a vital role in facilitating a learning, inclusive, and academically supportive residential community at Indiana Tech. This position supports the mission of Student Affairs and Residence Life by promoting student development, leadership, and student success through programming, leadership development, and administrative oversight. Responsibilities below may rotate between primary and secondary roles, based upon experience, expertise and departmental goals. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Student Engagement & Community Development Demonstrate active support for Student Affairs and Residence Life initiatives. Cultivate a residential experience that promotes belonging, respect, academic success, and student retention. Assist residents in resolving interpersonal conflicts and navigating developmental challenges. Serve as a role model and mentor to students, promoting leadership and personal growth. Resident Assistant (RA) Leadership Recruit, train, and supervise RA staff, providing consistent individual and team meetings focused on leadership, interpersonal skills, and team cohesion. Maintain professional and RA on-call rotation schedule. Provide ongoing training and development to enhance RA effectiveness. Develop and implement programming that supports community development and co-curricular learning. Housing Operations & Facilities Management Oversee housing operations and online program (StarRez) across all residential facilities. Coordinate room assignments, room changes, check-in/check-out procedures, and maintain accurate housing records. Conduct regular inspections of residential areas and report maintenance issues. Collaborate with Building & Grounds, Housekeeping, and Campus Safety to maintain safe and well-functioning living environments. Administrative Oversight Manage area budgets and support programming efforts aligned with departmental learning outcomes. Maintain compliance with University policies including FERPA, hazing, and Title IX. Assist with summer housing needs, including camp placements, key distribution, and supervision. Assessment & Strategic Collaboration Assess departmental learning outcomes and contribute to continuous improvement efforts. Work closely with the Director of Residence Life to meet or exceed student retention and occupancy goals. Collaborate with campus partners to inform and educate students about university procedures and available resources. Perform additional duties assigned to support the mission of Residence Life and Student Affairs. Support the mission, just cause, and strategic plan of Indiana Institute of Technology. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; master’s degree in Higher Education, Student Development or other related field preferred Competence in relational, interactive, and conflict mediation skills Competence in administrative, teambuilding and organizational skills Demonstrated consciousness of diversity, equity, and inclusion Experience 2-3 years of progressive leadership experience working with college students Working Conditions Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment and frequently in residence halls and various campus locations.  Evening and weekend hours are required for campus events and various activities. Application materials must include a cover letter and resume. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's vision and diversity statements. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/282584": {
      "title": "Director of Curriculum Design & AI Integration",
      "description": "Director of Curriculum Design & AI Integration You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Curriculum Design & AI Integration Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Doctorate Degree Preferred Category Artificial Intelligence Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech is seeking a strategic, innovative, and collaborative leader to serve as its next Director of Curriculum Design & AI Integration. Reporting to the Executive Director of the AI Institute, this position provides leadership for curriculum design, instructional innovation, and AI integration across the university. The Director serves as the bridge between faculty ideas and implementation, transforming innovative pedagogical concepts into high-quality, AI-enabled learning experiences that advance student success and academic excellence. The Director of Curriculum Design & AI Integration is responsible for overseeing institution-wide curriculum design standards, structures, and processes, including AI literacy competencies and AI integration guidelines for courses and academic programs. This position works closely with faculty, academic leadership, instructional designers, and learning technologists to ensure that curriculum innovation aligns with institutional goals, accreditation requirements, and emerging best practices in teaching and learning. The successful candidate will lead the university’s curriculum redesign operation by supervising the Curriculum Project Manager as well as teams of Learning Designers and Learning Technologists. The Director will establish processes, workflows, professional-development pathways, and quality standards that support scalable course redesign and continuous instructional improvement across academic programs. Working closely with the AI Faculty Strategist, the Director will receive faculty-generated redesign initiatives and translate pedagogical goals into structured, resourced curriculum projects. This role will oversee the development, implementation, quality assurance, accessibility review, and AI-integration standards for redesigned courses before launch. The Director will also partner with academic deans, program chairs, and accreditation leaders to ensure curriculum initiatives advance program-level outcomes and institutional priorities. Additional responsibilities include monitoring emerging instructional design practices, evaluating innovations in AI-enabled learning, reporting redesign outcomes and curriculum metrics, and supporting strategic initiatives associated with the university’s AI Institute and grant activities. Required Skills and Experience The ideal candidate will possess a master’s degree in instructional design, curriculum and instruction, educational technology, higher education, computer science, artificial intelligence, or a related field, along with a minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in instructional design, curriculum development, educational innovation, or higher education leadership. Candidates must demonstrate a strong understanding of curriculum development, instructional design principles, and the integration of artificial intelligence into teaching and learning environments. The successful candidate will have experience leading instructional design initiatives and creating systems that support high-quality, scalable curriculum development. The position requires demonstrated experience supervising instructional designers, learning technologists, or similar professional teams. Candidates must possess strong project-management, quality-assurance, organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and collaborate effectively with faculty and academic leaders across disciplines. Experience with learning management systems, course development platforms, and quality-review processes is required. The successful candidate must also be able to translate educational goals into effective course designs while ensuring consistency, accessibility, and instructional quality across academic offerings. Preferred Skills and Experience A doctoral degree in instructional design, curriculum and instruction, educational technology, higher education, artificial intelligence, computer science, or a related field is preferred. Preferred candidates will have experience integrating artificial intelligence or other emerging educational technologies into curriculum design and course development. Experience working with accreditation, assessment, academic quality-review processes, or program evaluation initiatives is also highly desirable. Additional preferred qualifications include experience leading large-scale curriculum transformation initiatives, developing instructional design standards, establishing quality-assurance frameworks, creating professional-development programs for instructional teams, and supporting grant-funded innovation projects. Opportunity and Impact This is an exciting opportunity for a visionary curriculum leader to influence the future of teaching and learning at Indiana Tech. The Director of Curriculum Design & AI Integration will help shape how artificial intelligence is incorporated into academic programs, create scalable processes that support instructional excellence, and develop innovative learning experiences that prepare students for an AI-enabled workforce. Success in this role will be measured through the number and quality of courses and programs redesigned, faculty satisfaction with the redesign process, consistency of instructional design standards, accreditation alignment, effectiveness of curriculum workflows, professional growth of the Learning Designer and Learning Technologist teams, and achievement of curriculum-related grant milestones. Why Indiana Tech? Indiana Tech is a private, nonprofit university committed to innovation, collaboration, and student success. As a member of the AI Institute leadership team, the Director of Curriculum Design & AI Integration will have the opportunity to shape the future of curriculum innovation, influence teaching and learning across the university, and help position Indiana Tech as a leader in responsible AI-enhanced education. Ready to help design the future of higher education? Apply today and join Indiana Tech in creating innovative, AI-integrated learning experiences that empower faculty, engage students, and advance academic excellence. **Application materials must include Vita and unofficial transcripts. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/282578": {
      "title": "Warrior AI Readiness Manager",
      "description": "Warrior AI Readiness Manager You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Warrior AI Readiness Manager Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Doctorate Degree Preferred Category Artificial Intelligence Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech is seeking an innovative, collaborative, and forward-thinking professional to serve as its Warrior AI Readiness Manager. Reporting to the Executive Director of the AI Institute, this position leads Indiana Tech’s institution-wide artificial intelligence professional development strategy for faculty and staff. The Warrior AI Readiness Manager is responsible for building the infrastructure, resources, programming, and assessment tools that support AI readiness across the university and help create a culture of responsible, effective, and innovative AI adoption. The Warrior AI Readiness Manager serves as the architect and steward of Indiana Tech’s faculty and staff AI learning ecosystem. This includes oversight of the Warrior AI Digital Learning Hub, the university’s AI professional development programming calendar, AI-readiness assessments, learning analytics, recognition initiatives, and ongoing training opportunities designed to strengthen AI knowledge, confidence, and application across the institution. Working closely with the AI Faculty Strategist, Human Resources, Information Technology, and academic leadership, the Manager develops and delivers AI-focused workshops, seminars, retreats, communities of practice, and professional development experiences for faculty and staff. This role also supports institution-wide AI tool adoption, coordinates learning and readiness assessment efforts, and ensures programming remains aligned with emerging technologies, institutional priorities, and grant objectives. The Warrior AI Readiness Manager will oversee faculty and staff AI-readiness surveys and analytics, using data to identify development opportunities and guide institutional decision-making. The position also manages Warrior AI Shorts and other recognition programs that highlight innovative faculty and staff uses of AI and promote the sharing of effective practices across campus. Through partnerships with Human Resources and Information Technology, the Manager will help embed AI competencies into onboarding, professional development, and operational improvement initiatives. The successful candidate will monitor emerging AI trends, assess program effectiveness, support grant-related reporting and outcomes, and champion ethical, responsible, and secure AI use throughout the university. Required Skills and Experience The ideal candidate will possess a master’s degree in educational technology, instructional design, higher education, organizational development, computer science, business, or a related field. Candidates must have a minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in higher education, organizational development, instructional design, professional learning, or related fields. Candidates must demonstrate a strong understanding of generative AI technologies and their application in higher education, workforce development, and organizational learning environments. The successful candidate will possess the ability to translate complex AI concepts into practical, engaging learning experiences for faculty and staff with varying levels of experience and technical expertise. The position requires demonstrated success designing and delivering large-scale professional development, training, or organizational learning programs. Candidates must possess exceptional communication, facilitation, presentation, project management, and interpersonal skills, along with the ability to manage multiple initiatives and engage stakeholders across all areas of the university. Experience designing and delivering both online and face-to-face learning experiences is required, as is experience supporting organizational change initiatives and helping individuals adopt new tools, practices, and technologies. Preferred Skills and Experience A doctoral degree in educational technology, instructional design, higher education, organizational development, computer science, business, or a related field is preferred. Preferred candidates will have experience working with learning management systems, digital learning platforms, learning analytics, and assessment tools used to evaluate professional development effectiveness. Experience with program assessment, continuous improvement processes, and data-informed decision-making is also highly desirable. Additional preferred qualifications include experience developing institution-wide learning initiatives, implementing workforce readiness or technology adoption programs, creating digital learning resources, and supporting grant-funded educational or organizational transformation projects. Opportunity and Impact This is an exciting opportunity for a strategic learning and development leader to help shape how Indiana Tech prepares faculty and staff for an AI-enabled future. The Warrior AI Readiness Manager will play a critical role in building institutional AI capacity, strengthening workforce readiness, and creating development experiences that empower faculty and staff to leverage AI confidently, responsibly, and effectively. Success in this role will be measured through faculty and staff participation and satisfaction with AI professional development, growth and utilization of the Warrior AI Digital Learning Hub, improvements in AI-readiness survey results, increased integration of AI into workflows and teaching practices, achievement of grant milestones, and continuous improvement driven by assessment data. Why Indiana Tech? Indiana Tech is a private, nonprofit university dedicated to innovation, collaboration, and student success. As a member of the AI Institute leadership team, the Warrior AI Readiness Manager will help create the learning culture, development infrastructure, and institutional capabilities necessary to ensure Indiana Tech remains a leader in responsible and effective AI adoption across higher education. Ready to help build a campus-wide culture of AI readiness and innovation? Apply today and join Indiana Tech in preparing faculty and staff to lead, learn, and succeed in an increasingly AI-enabled world. **Applicants should submit a cover letter and résumé. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Indiana Tech's mission and vision. The position will remain open until filled; review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/282562": {
      "title": "AI Faculty Strategist",
      "description": "AI Faculty Strategist You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account AI Faculty Strategist Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Doctorate Degree Preferred Category Artificial Intelligence Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech is seeking an innovative, collaborative, and faculty-centered leader to serve as its AI Faculty Strategist. Reporting to the Executive Director of the AI Institute, with a dotted-line relationship to the Vice President for Academic Affairs, this position serves as the university’s primary faculty consultant for artificial intelligence pedagogy and instructional innovation. The AI Faculty Strategist leads Indiana Tech’s faculty-facing initiative for teaching AI within the curriculum and helps faculty build the knowledge, confidence, and instructional judgment needed to effectively integrate AI into teaching and learning. Serving concurrently as Director of the Teaching Excellence Center, the AI Faculty Strategist plays a central role in advancing Indiana Tech’s institutional AI strategy by helping faculty navigate the rapidly evolving landscape of artificial intelligence in higher education. This position works closely with the Warrior AI Readiness Manager, the Director of Curriculum Design & AI Integration, academic deans, instructional designers, and faculty across disciplines to move instructors from AI awareness to meaningful course and program transformation. The AI Faculty Strategist serves as the primary point of contact for faculty seeking guidance on AI pedagogy, instructional design, assessment redesign, and responsible AI integration. The successful candidate will provide individual consultation, facilitate professional development opportunities, mentor faculty participating in AI innovation initiatives, and help faculty identify opportunities for course redesign and instructional improvement. Faculty projects selected for full redesign and implementation will be carried out in partnership with the Curriculum Design team. Additional responsibilities include developing and facilitating workshops, seminars, communities of practice, and faculty-development programs focused on AI in higher education. The Strategist will use institutional readiness data to identify coaching opportunities, contribute faculty-focused programming to university-wide AI initiatives, create instructional resources and teaching guides, support grant-related activities, and represent Indiana Tech’s AI efforts at institutional, regional, and national conferences. Required Skills and Experience The ideal candidate will possess a master’s degree in education, educational technology, instructional design, higher education, computer science, artificial intelligence, business, or a related discipline, along with a minimum of five years of higher-education teaching experience. Candidates must demonstrate a strong understanding of artificial intelligence applications in higher education, including their impact on teaching, learning, assessment, curriculum design, and student engagement. The successful candidate will have a record of instructional innovation and experience integrating emerging educational technologies into academic programs and classroom environments. The position requires demonstrated excellence in college teaching, outstanding written and verbal communication skills, and the ability to engage faculty from a wide variety of academic disciplines. Candidates must possess strong consultation, facilitation, coaching, and presentation skills and be able to foster collaboration while supporting faculty through instructional change and innovation. Experience in designing and facilitating faculty development programs, workshops, training sessions, or professional learning initiatives is required. Candidates should also demonstrate the ability to translate complex AI concepts into practical instructional strategies that can be implemented effectively in diverse academic settings. Preferred Skills and Experience A doctoral degree in education, instructional design, higher education, educational technology, artificial intelligence, computer science, business, or a related discipline is preferred. Preferred candidates will have scholarship related to teaching and learning, educational technology, instructional innovation, or artificial intelligence. Experience supporting online education, digital learning environments, and faculty adoption of emerging technologies is also highly desirable. Additional preferred qualifications include experience leading institutional teaching and learning initiatives, developing instructional resources and toolkits, presenting at professional conferences, managing faculty innovation programs, or supporting grant-funded educational projects. Opportunity and Impact This is an exciting opportunity for a passionate educator and thought leader to help shape the future of teaching and learning at Indiana Tech. The AI Faculty Strategist will play a critical role in helping faculty understand, evaluate, and responsibly integrate artificial intelligence into their courses while strengthening student learning outcomes and preparing graduates for an AI-enabled workforce. Success in this role will be reflected through increased faculty participation in AI professional development, growth in faculty consultations and curriculum redesign activity, development of instructional resources and teaching guides, improvement in AI-informed teaching practices, scholarly contributions, conference presentations, and achievement of grant-supported initiatives. Why Indiana Tech? Indiana Tech is a private, nonprofit university dedicated to innovation, collaboration, and student success. As part of the AI Institute and Teaching Excellence Center, the AI Faculty Strategist will have the opportunity to influence teaching practices across the university and help position Indiana Tech as a leader in responsible and effective AI integration in higher education. Ready to help faculty transform teaching and learning for the age of artificial intelligence? Apply today and join Indiana Tech in shaping the future of higher education through innovation, collaboration, and instructional excellence. **Application materials must include Vita and unofficial transcripts. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/282557": {
      "title": "Institutional Intelligent Operations Manager",
      "description": "Institutional Intelligent Operations Manager You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Institutional Intelligent Operations Manager Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Master's Degree Preferred Category Artificial Intelligence Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech is seeking an innovative, analytical, and collaborative professional to serve as its Institutional Intelligent Operations Manager. Reporting to the Executive Director of the AI Institute, this position will lead the responsible adoption of artificial intelligence-enabled tools, automation, and analytics across Indiana Tech’s academic and administrative operations. The Institutional Intelligent Operations Manager serves as the operational bridge connecting the AI Institute, the Learning Exchange, Information Technology, and university departments to identify, evaluate, implement, and scale technology solutions that improve efficiency, decision-making, and the overall institutional experience. This role serves as the technical and operational backbone behind several of Indiana Tech’s strategic AI initiatives, including the Warrior AI Digital Learning Hub, readiness-survey analytics, curriculum evaluation platforms, Learning Exchange systems, and Employer Portal technologies. The successful candidate will help ensure that AI-powered solutions are implemented responsibly, securely, and in compliance with university policies and regulatory requirements. Primary responsibilities include identifying opportunities for AI-enabled automation and analytics, evaluating new technologies and vendors, managing intelligent-operations pilot projects, and collaborating with campus stakeholders to redesign processes around AI-assisted tools. The Manager will oversee projects from concept through implementation, helping departments realize operational efficiencies, improve services, and strengthen data-informed decision-making. The Institutional Intelligent Operations Manager serves as the AI Institute’s operational liaison to Information Technology and the University AI Council, evaluating AI tools and vendors for privacy, security, and compliance risks prior to implementation. This position will maintain the university’s inventory of AI tools and their associated data flows, support institutional compliance reviews, establish dashboards and performance metrics, provide change-management support, and monitor emerging technologies that may benefit Indiana Tech. Working collaboratively with leaders across Academic Affairs, Human Resources, Finance, Enrollment Services, Information Technology, the Learning Exchange, and the AI Institute, the Manager will help drive innovative solutions that support both academic and operational excellence. The position also contributes to staff development, supports strategic initiatives, and advances Indiana Tech’s mission, vision, and strategic plan. Required Skills and Experience The ideal candidate will possess a bachelor’s degree in information technology, business administration, data analytics, operations, or a related field, along with a minimum of five years of progressively responsible experience in higher education administration, information technology, operations, process improvement, or project leadership. Candidates must demonstrate a strong understanding of generative AI technologies, automation tools, and analytics platforms, as well as their administrative and academic applications. The successful candidate must understand data-privacy, cybersecurity, and compliance considerations associated with emerging technologies, particularly within higher education environments. The position requires demonstrated experience leading cross-functional projects, implementing process improvements, and managing initiatives involving diverse stakeholder groups. Candidates must possess strong organizational, project-management, vendor-evaluation, written communication, and presentation skills, as well as the ability to translate complex technical concepts into practical solutions for non-technical audiences. Experience evaluating, implementing, or scaling AI-enabled tools, automation technologies, or analytics platforms across multiple business functions is required. Candidates should also demonstrate the ability to build consensus and guide change across departments with different priorities and operational needs. Preferred Skills and Experience A master’s degree in information technology, business administration, data analytics, organizational leadership, or a related field is preferred. Additional preferred qualifications include experience working with FERPA, GLBA, or similar data-privacy and compliance frameworks; experience managing technology vendors and procurement processes; and familiarity with institutional governance, data management, and technology assessment practices. Preference will also be given to candidates who have successfully led digital-transformation initiatives, developed operational dashboards and analytics frameworks, implemented AI-enabled business processes, or supported large-scale organizational change efforts involving technology adoption. Opportunity and Impact This is an exciting opportunity for a forward-thinking professional to help shape how Indiana Tech responsibly adopts and scales artificial intelligence across the institution. The Institutional Intelligent Operations Manager will play a central role in improving operational efficiency, strengthening compliance and governance practices, and enabling faculty and staff to leverage emerging technologies in meaningful and sustainable ways. Success in this role will be measured by the number and impact of intelligent-operations projects successfully scaled into standard practice, documented operational improvements, successful AI compliance reviews, adoption of AI-enabled workflows, and the ongoing maintenance of institutional AI governance and reporting systems. Why Indiana Tech? Indiana Tech is a private, nonprofit university committed to innovation, collaboration, and student success. This position offers the opportunity to work at the intersection of technology, operations, and higher education while helping build a university-wide approach to responsible artificial intelligence adoption and intelligent operations. Ready to help transform the future of higher education operations through responsible AI innovation? Apply today and join Indiana Tech in building smarter, more efficient, and more impactful ways of serving students, employees, and the broader university community. **Applicants should submit a cover letter and résumé. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Indiana Tech's mission and vision. The position will remain open until filled; review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/282551": {
      "title": "Executive Director, AI Institute",
      "description": "Executive Director, AI Institute You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Executive Director, AI Institute Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Doctorate Degree Preferred Category Artificial Intelligence Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech is seeking a visionary, collaborative, and results-driven leader to serve as its Executive Director of the AI Institute. Reporting to the Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Executive Director will provide strategic vision and operational leadership for Indiana Tech’s AI Institute. This position will build a coordinated pathway that moves faculty, staff, and students from AI awareness to hands-on curriculum redesign while positioning Indiana Tech as a regional leader in the responsible adoption of artificial intelligence in higher education. The Executive Director will establish the Institute’s strategic vision, annual priorities, and multi-year roadmap in alignment with Indiana Tech’s Strategic Plan. This leader will oversee the Institute’s faculty AI-development pipeline, spanning awareness, coaching, and curriculum execution, and will supervise a multidisciplinary team responsible for AI readiness, faculty strategy, curriculum design and integration, regional partnerships, and intelligent institutional operations The Executive Director will serve as principal administrator for any future grants, with responsibility for budget oversight, milestone tracking, funder reporting, and renewal or expansion proposals. This position will also oversee the Institute’s operating and grant budgets and establish shared metrics and reporting tools that clearly communicate progress across the AI-development pipeline. As the Institute’s principal liaison to the University AI Council, the Executive Director will ensure that programs, tools, and data practices align with Indiana Tech’s Artificial Intelligence Policy and applicable FERPA, GLBA, and data-governance obligations. This leader will convene and chair an AI Institute Advisory Board composed of academic deans, faculty, Information Technology, and Human Resources representatives to establish priorities and review new AI tools before campus-wide implementation. The Executive Director will build regional employer and community partnerships, represent the AI Institute to grantors, accreditors, and external funders, and monitor the national AI-in-higher-education landscape to inform institutional priorities. Additional responsibilities include leading change-management and communication efforts, publishing an annual “State of AI at Indiana Tech” report, sponsoring a faculty AI fellows or seed-grant program, and supporting the hiring, onboarding, and performance management of Institute employees. Required Skills and Experience The successful candidate will possess a master’s degree in higher education administration, educational technology, computer science, artificial intelligence, business, or a related field. Candidates must have at least seven years of progressively responsible leadership experience in higher education, including experience supervising professional staff and managing budgets and personnel. Candidates must demonstrate a strong understanding of generative AI technologies, their applications in higher education, and the related risks and compliance considerations, including FERPA, GLBA, and data governance. The position requires the ability to balance innovation with responsible technology adoption and to translate complex technical, academic, and compliance matters for varied institutional audiences. Experience administering grant-funded programs, including budget oversight and funder reporting, is required. Candidates must also have experience developing partnerships with external organizations, such as employers, community organizations, or regional and national networks. The successful candidate will possess outstanding written, verbal, and executive presentation skills and be prepared to represent Indiana Tech with external partners and interested parties. Candidates must demonstrate the ability to build consensus and advance complex initiatives across academic and administrative units with competing priorities. Preferred Skills and Experience A doctoral degree in higher education administration, educational technology, computer science, artificial intelligence, business, or a related field is preferred. Preferred candidates will have experience leading institutional AI, educational technology, or digital-transformation initiatives. Experience working with or reporting to institutional governance and policy bodies, such as data-governance or AI-governance committees, is also preferred. Additional preferred experience includes leading organizational change associated with emerging technologies, developing institution-wide professional learning initiatives, supporting responsible AI adoption, and building partnerships that connect higher education with employer and community needs. Opportunity and Impact This is an exciting opportunity for a forward-thinking leader to shape the strategy, infrastructure, and culture surrounding artificial intelligence at Indiana Tech. The Executive Director will help faculty, staff, and students develop confidence and competency in using AI, support the redesign of courses and academic programs, strengthen regional partnerships, and establish the systems needed for ethical, secure, and sustainable AI adoption. Success will be reflected in the achievement of grant milestones; growth in faculty and staff AI readiness; the number of courses and programs redesigned with AI integration; regional partnership agreements and their workforce impact; compliance reviews completed without significant findings; faculty, staff, and student satisfaction; and the successful publication of the annual “State of AI at Indiana Tech” report. Why Indiana Tech? Indiana Tech is a private, nonprofit university committed to career-focused education, innovation, collaboration, and student success. The Executive Director will join a mission-focused academic leadership team and have the opportunity to guide the responsible use of an emerging technology that will influence teaching, learning, workforce preparation, and institutional operations. Ready to shape the future of responsible AI adoption in higher education? Apply today and help Indiana Tech build an innovative, ethical, and collaborative approach to artificial intelligence that prepares students, faculty, staff, and regional partners for what comes next. **Application materials must include Vita and unofficial transcripts. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/282516": {
      "title": "Regional AI Partnerships Manager",
      "description": "Regional AI Partnerships Manager You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Regional AI Partnerships Manager Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Master's Degree Preferred Category Artificial Intelligence Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech invites applications for the position of Regional AI Partnerships Manager within The Learning Exchange. Reporting to the Director of the Learning Exchange, with a dotted-line relationship to the Executive Director of the AI Institute, this position serves as a key connector between Indiana Tech, regional employers, workforce organizations, and community partners. The Regional AI Partnerships Manager will build and manage employer relationships that support applied AI projects, workforce development initiatives, corporate training opportunities, and industry engagement for both The Learning Exchange and the AI Institute. The successful candidate will represent Indiana Tech across the region, maintain strategic partnerships, and connect employers to AI readiness, workforce training, and talent-development programs. The Regional AI Partnerships Manager will collaborate closely with AI Institute leadership, community organizations, workforce boards, economic-development partners, and employer networks to identify emerging workforce needs and expand opportunities for students and organizations. Responsibilities include developing employer partnerships, supporting corporate training agreements, coordinating employer engagement activities, monitoring partnership outcomes, and helping grow regional participation in AI-focused education and workforce initiatives. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Business, Marketing, Economic Development, Higher Education Administration, or a related field; a minimum of five years of experience in employer relations, business development, workforce partnerships, or a related field; demonstrated experience building and maintaining external partnerships; strong understanding of employer needs, workforce development trends, and regional labor markets; and exceptional relationship-building, communication, negotiation, and presentation skills. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in a related discipline; experience negotiating corporate contracts, subscriptions, or licensing agreements; experience with CRM, employer engagement, or partnership management systems; and experience coordinating partnerships across multiple institutions, organizations, or consortium structures. Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-focused education in a wide variety of disciplines. We are committed to preparing students for success through innovative academic programs, experiential learning opportunities, and strong connections with industry and community partners. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Opportunity and Impact This is an opportunity for an innovative leader to shape a university-wide and regionally connected learning enterprise. The Director will help expand access to workforce learning and professional education, strengthen pathways between non-credit and credit-bearing learning, cultivate meaningful employer partnerships, and build sustainable systems that serve learners, faculty, employers, and consortium institutions. Why Indiana Tech? Indiana Tech is a private, nonprofit university committed to career-focused education, innovation, collaboration, and student success. The Director will join a mission-focused academic leadership team and have the opportunity to build programs and partnerships that respond directly to evolving learner, employer, and regional workforce needs. Ready to help shape the future of workforce learning, professional education, and regional collaboration? Apply today and join Indiana Tech in creating meaningful and accessible learning pathways for students, working professionals, and employers. ** Applicants should submit a cover letter and résumé. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Indiana Tech's mission and vision. The position will remain open until filled; review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/282504": {
      "title": "Director of the Learning Exchange",
      "description": "Director of the Learning Exchange You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of the Learning Exchange Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Doctorate Degree Preferred Category Artificial Intelligence Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech is seeking a strategic, entrepreneurial, and collaborative leader to serve as its Director of the Learning Exchange. Reporting to the Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Director will provide operational and business leadership for the Learning Exchange, Indiana Tech’s coordinated enterprise for workforce learning, executive and leadership education, professional development, academic readiness, student success, and academic pathways. The Director will set the strategic direction for the Learning Exchange portfolio, balancing revenue, enrollment, and mission-focused outcomes. This position will lead the Learning Exchange Operations team, establish pricing and revenue-allocation frameworks for non-credit offerings, manage the portfolio’s financial performance, and develop corporate training contracts and learning subscriptions. The Director will convene a cross-functional steering committee involving Academic Affairs, Information Technology, Finance, Marketing and Enrollment, and Institutional Effectiveness to establish priorities and address issues that span university departments. The Director will play an important role in connecting credit and non-credit learning experiences across the Learning Exchange. This includes helping build a unified learner identity and record, along with shared services supporting registration, payment, credentialing, and analytics. The Director will also support the hiring, onboarding, and performance management of staff and contribute to the mission, vision, and strategic plan of Indiana Tech. Required Skills and Experience The successful candidate will possess a master’s degree in higher education administration, business, educational technology, or a related field, along with at least seven years of progressively responsible leadership experience in higher education, workforce development, or continuing or professional education. Experience must include the supervision of professional staff and demonstrated success building or scaling a workforce-learning, professional development, or continuing-education enterprise, including responsibility for business-model development and portfolio management. Candidates must have experience administering large, grant-funded, multi-institution initiatives, including budget oversight, milestone management, compliance, and funder reporting. The position also requires experience developing employer or industry partnerships and negotiating corporate training, subscription, or licensing agreements. A strong understanding of consortium coordination and employer-facing partnership development is essential. The ideal candidate will demonstrate excellent strategic, financial, organizational, and relationship-management skills, with the ability to lead complex initiatives involving academic leaders, university departments, external partners, employers, and multiple institutions. Outstanding written, verbal, and executive presentation skills are required, as is the ability to build consensus and move work forward among stakeholders with differing priorities. Preferred Skills and Experience A doctoral degree in higher education administration, business, educational technology, or a related field is preferred. Additional preferred experience includes working with online learning platforms, customer relationship management systems, digital credentialing, learner records, enterprise learning services, and multi-institution consortium or governance structures. Preference will be given to candidates who have demonstrated success developing sustainable revenue models for education or workforce-learning programs; leading cross-functional teams; building regional employer partnerships; and using enrollment, revenue, learner-outcome, and employer-engagement data to guide decisions. Experience supporting artificial intelligence education, applied-learning initiatives, digital transformation, or regional workforce-development partnerships would further strengthen a candidate’s qualifications. Opportunity and Impact This is an opportunity for an innovative leader to shape a university-wide and regionally connected learning enterprise. The Director will help expand access to workforce learning and professional education, strengthen pathways between non-credit and credit-bearing learning, cultivate meaningful employer partnerships, and build sustainable systems that serve learners, faculty, employers, and consortium institutions. Why Indiana Tech? Indiana Tech is a private, nonprofit university committed to career-focused education, innovation, collaboration, and student success. The Director will join a mission-focused academic leadership team and have the opportunity to build programs and partnerships that respond directly to evolving learner, employer, and regional workforce needs. Ready to help shape the future of workforce learning, professional education, and regional collaboration? Apply today and join Indiana Tech in creating meaningful and accessible learning pathways for students, working professionals, and employers. **Application materials must include Vita and unofficial transcripts. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/279610": {
      "title": "Transfer Admissions Counselor - Traditional Day",
      "description": "Transfer Admissions Counselor - Traditional Day You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Transfer Admissions Counselor - Traditional Day Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Bachelor's Degree Preferred Category Admissions/Recruiting Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu Reporting to the Executive Director of Admissions, the Transfer Admissions Counselor is responsible for recruiting, counseling, and enrolling prospective transfer students into Indiana Tech’s traditional undergraduate programs. This position serves as the primary point of contact for transfer students throughout the admissions process, including application review, transfer credit evaluation coordination, financial aid guidance, and enrollment advising The Transfer Admissions Counselor develops and maintains relationships with community colleges, faculty, staff, and external partners to facilitate transfer pathways and increase transfer student enrollment. The position works collaboratively with the Transfer Advisor in the Office of Student Success and other campus partners to support a seamless transition from admission through enrollment, promote student success, and enhance the overall transfer student experience. Work will be performed in a manner that contributes to the university’s enrollment objectives while supporting Indiana Tech’s mission, vision, and values. The Transfer Admissions Counselor serves as an active member of the Indiana Tech Transfer Task Force and collaborates across campus to improve transfer processes, strengthen partnerships, and advance initiatives that support transfer student recruitment, enrollment, and success Essential Duties & Responsibilities Transfer Recruitment and Enrollment Recruit prospective transfer students through in-person appointments, phone calls, text messaging, email communications, virtual meetings, and admissions events. Manage transfer recruitment and develop strategies to increase transfer student enrollment. Build and maintain relationships with community colleges, academic advisors, faculty, and transfer coordinators. Represent Indiana Tech at transfer fairs, community college visits, campus events, and other recruitment activities. Assist transfer students through the admissions, financial aid, and enrollment processes. Conduct individual counseling sessions with students regarding transfer opportunities, degree programs, costs, and scholarship options. Develop and execute transfer-specific communication and recruitment plans designed to generate applications, deposits, and enrollments. Transfer Credit Evaluation and Admissions Review Request, monitor, and coordinate transfer credit evaluations with the Transfer Advisor and other campus partners. Review completed transfer evaluations with students and explain degree applicability, remaining requirements, and graduation pathways. Conduct preliminary reviews of transcripts and admissions documents to determine admissions eligibility and application readiness. Make admissions recommendations and decisions in accordance with institutional policies and established admission standards. Advocate for students to maximize transferability of previously earned coursework. Complete transcript reviews, transfer credit evaluations, admissions evaluations, application processing, and other enrollment-related duties as needed during peak application and enrollment periods. Student Success Collaboration Collaborate closely with the Transfer Advisor in the Office of Student Success to support a seamless transition for transfer students from admission through enrollment and persistence. Coordinate regularly regarding transfer student needs, academic planning, registration readiness, and student support services. Partner with the Transfer Advisor to identify and address barriers to enrollment, retention, and student success. Participate in joint outreach efforts and initiatives designed to improve the transfer student experience and increase student persistence. Share relevant student information and enrollment updates in accordance with institutional policies to ensure continuity of support throughout the student lifecycle. Indiana Tech Transfer Task Force Serve as an active member of the Indiana Tech Transfer Task Force. Collaborate with campus partners to identify opportunities to improve transfer student recruitment, enrollment, retention, and graduation outcomes. Assist in the development and implementation of transfer initiatives, articulation agreements, policies, and procedures. Provide feedback and recommendations based on transfer student trends, challenges, and enrollment data. Support institutional efforts to create and enhance transfer pathways that improve student access and success. Team Collaboration and Operational Support Participate in admissions events including visit programs, open houses, accepted student events, orientation activities, and transfer-specific programs. Assist with recruitment travel, presentations, and outreach initiatives as assigned. Support departmental recruitment initiatives and collaborate with admissions staff to ensure enrollment goals are achieved. Contribute to a positive team environment and assist with special projects and additional responsibilities as assigned. Adhere to all university, state, and federal regulations related to student recruitment and admissions practices Measures of Accomplishment Achievement of individual and departmental transfer enrollment goals. Growth in transfer applications, admits, deposits, and enrolled students. Timely completion of transfer credit evaluations and admissions decisions. Development and maintenance of community college partnerships and transfer pathways. Effective participation and contribution to the Indiana Tech Transfer Task Force. Accurate and timely documentation of student interactions within Slate CRM. Positive service and responsiveness to students, families, and campus partners Qualifications Required Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to travel and maintain insurability under university requirements. Preferred Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications and Slate CRM, preferred. Previous experience in admissions, higher education, recruitment, sales, customer service, or transfer student services, preferred. Familiarity with transfer credit evaluation processes, articulation agreements, and student success initiatives, preferred. Experience Two years or more work experience within admissions is preferred, and bachelor’s degree required. Application materials must include a cover letter and resume. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/279124": {
      "title": "Financial Systems Accountant",
      "description": "Financial Systems Accountant You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Financial Systems Accountant Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Bachelor's Category Accounting Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan . Indiana Tech is seeking a forward-thinking Financial Systems Accountant to join our finance team on the Fort Wayne campus. The Financial Systems Accountant combines expertise in accounting, financial reporting, data analytics, and technology to support and enhance the university's financial operations. This position works closely with other university departments, leadership, and external vendors to ensure financial systems accurately support accounting transactions, financial processes, financial reporting, internal controls, and data governance. The position is responsible for maintaining and optimizing financial applications/systems, developing automated reports and dashboards, improving business processes through technology solutions, and ensuring the integrity and reliability of financial data across multiple systems. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Accounting, Financial Reporting & Data Analytics Perform and support month-end and year-end close processes, including journal entries, reconciliations, and variance analysis. Prepare and analyze monthly and annual financial statements in accordance with GAAP and regulatory standards. Review financial data for accuracy, completeness, and compliance with accounting standards and university policies. Perform balance sheet account reconciliations and investigate discrepancies Assists with budgeting and forecasting processes. Support audit requests by providing documentation, data analyses, and system process information. Provide financial data for external surveys and reports. Develop and maintain dashboards and reports that support cash management, accounts receivable, accounts payable, fixed assets, and general ledger activities and monitor financial performance and KPIs. Analyze large datasets to identify trends, anomalies, and opportunities for cost savings or revenue enhancement. Maintain internal database files and tables and develop custom reports/queries to meet the needs of the finance department and university leadership. Collaborate with departments to ensure accurate financial coding and reporting. Monitor system processes that impact accounting transactions and recommend improvements when issues are identified. Ensure financial system configurations support proper accounting treatment and reporting requirements. Systems Administration & Automation Serve as a subject matter expert and collaborate with university departments to integrate and automate financial systems. Manage internal and external system upgrades, integrations, configurations, user permissions, and data integrity across platforms. Ensure systems comply with financial regulations and internal controls. Monitor system performance and conduct regular audits. Troubleshoot system issues and work with IT, university departments, and vendors to resolve problems. Participate in system and process re-engineering efforts and automation. Process Improvement & Optimization Identify opportunities to streamline financial processes and workflows to enhance accuracy, efficiency, and scalability. Develop reconciliation processes to ensure reporting consistency. Utilize tools such as Power Query, Power BI, Power Automate, Vena, and other technologies to improve operational efficiency. Conduct assessment of software and hardware needs and design new or modified systems to meet changing demands. Evaluate the impact of changes and recommend enhancements. Maintain documentation of procedures and develop training materials for system users and finance staff. Provide training and support to finance staff and departmental users on system functionality and best practices. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or related field. Advanced proficiency in Excel and experience with data visualization tools (e.g., Power BI, Power Query, pivot tables, lookups). Hands-on experience and knowledge with ERP, financial reporting, and automation platforms or AI agents (e.g., Jenzabar, Vena, Supervity, Microsoft 365). Broad knowledge of techniques in collecting data, analyzing information, generating reports,  or other data querying languages. Innovative with an eagerness to learn new processes and naturally curious. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills with intense attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Knowledge of financial internal controls and compliance frameworks. Self-starter and ability to work within a team, independently, and collaboratively across the university Experience 5+ years of progressive accounting experience, with at least 2-3 years in a data or systems-focused role. Working Conditions Work is typically performed in a standard office environment on university premises, with occasional travel. Some evening and weekend work may be required and/or necessary. Physical presence on campus during scheduled working hours is an essential function of this position. The employee must be able to consistently report to work on university premises, participate in in-person and remote meetings and activities, and perform duties requiring on-site access to university facilities, systems, records, and resources. Application materials must include a cover letter and resume. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/273304": {
      "title": "Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, and Smart Manufacturing Faculty",
      "description": "Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, and Smart Manufacturing Faculty You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, and Smart Manufacturing Faculty Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Doctorate Degree Preferred Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech invites applications for a full-time faculty member in Mechanical Engineering, Robotics and Smart Manufacturing to join the Talwar College of Engineering and Computer Sciences. This 12-month teaching faculty position offers an exciting opportunity to educate and mentor students while contributing to the continued growth of innovative engineering and technology programs. The successful candidate will possess expertise in multiple areas of mechanics, thermofluids, advanced manufacturing, robotics and automation, smart manufacturing systems, and emerging physical AI technologies. Preference will be given to candidates who can teach across multiple disciplines, including mechanical engineering, industrial and manufacturing engineering, mechatronics and robotics engineering, and mechanical engineering technology. This position may be filled as either a tenure-track faculty appointment or at the Professor of Practice rank, depending on the qualifications, academic credentials, and professional experience of the selected candidate. Faculty members teach in both face-to-face and online formats and play a critical role in advancing engineering education through innovative teaching, curriculum development, and student engagement. Responsibilities include developing new academic programs, enhancing existing curricula, advising and mentoring students, supporting student recruitment and retention initiatives, collaborating with colleagues across disciplines, and contributing to continuous program improvement efforts. Faculty are also expected to maintain academic records to support accreditation activities, participate in ABET assessment and continuous improvement processes, utilize learning management systems and instructional technologies effectively, and support the mission, vision, and strategic priorities of Indiana Tech. Qualified candidates must possess a master’s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, Manufacturing Engineering, or a closely related field, with a terminal degree preferred. Candidates with experience developing hands-on laboratory experiences, workforce training programs, or applied engineering curricula are especially encouraged to apply. Preference will be given to individuals with a demonstrated record of interdisciplinary collaboration across mechanics, engineering design, manufacturing systems, automation, or robotics. Experience with Fanuc robotics platforms, Industry 4.0 technologies, smart manufacturing systems, digital automation, or SACA-aligned curriculum development is highly desirable. College-level teaching experience and online teaching experience are preferred. Candidates should also demonstrate excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills as well as a strong commitment to student success and applied learning. Indiana Tech is a student-centered institution dedicated to providing career-focused education that prepares graduates to thrive in an advanced manufacturing and technology-driven economy. Located in Fort Wayne, Indiana, the university is recognized for its commitment to innovation, experiential learning, industry partnerships, and workforce development. Faculty enjoy the opportunity to work in a collaborative academic environment while helping shape the future of engineering, robotics, automation, and smart manufacturing education. **Application materials must include Vita and unofficial transcripts. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/273240": {
      "title": "Computer Science and Computer Engineering Faculty",
      "description": "Computer Science and Computer Engineering Faculty You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Computer Science and Computer Engineering Faculty Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Doctorate Degree Preferred Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . Indiana Tech invites applications for a full-time faculty member in Computer Science and Computer Engineering to join the Talwar College of Engineering and Computer Sciences. This 12-month teaching faculty position offers an exciting opportunity to educate and mentor students while contributing to the continued growth of innovative computing and engineering programs. The successful candidate will possess expertise in multiple areas of cybersecurity, computing, and artificial intelligence, with a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and student success. Preference will be given to candidates who can teach across multiple disciplines, including cybersecurity, artificial intelligence, computer science, computer engineering, and information systems. This position may be filled as either a tenure-track faculty appointment or at the Professor of Practice rank, depending on the qualifications, academic credentials, and professional experience of the selected candidate. Faculty members teach in both face-to-face and online formats and play a vital role in developing and enhancing academic programs that prepare students for successful careers in rapidly evolving technology fields. In addition to teaching, the successful candidate will contribute to curriculum development and continuous improvement initiatives, collaborate with faculty across disciplines, advise and mentor students, participate in recruitment and retention efforts, and support student engagement both inside and outside the classroom. Faculty are also expected to maintain academic records to support accreditation activities, leverage learning management systems and instructional technologies to enhance learning outcomes, and actively support the mission, vision, and strategic priorities of Indiana Tech. Qualified candidates must possess a master’s degree in Cybersecurity, Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or a closely related field, with a terminal degree preferred. Industry experience is highly valued, particularly for candidates seeking appointment as a Professor of Practice. Desired qualifications include college-level teaching experience, experience delivering online courses, and expertise in cybersecurity, computing, software development, networking, artificial intelligence, or related technical disciplines. Professional certifications such as CompTIA CySA+, Certified Ethical Hacker (CEH), Offensive Security Certified Professional (OSCP), Certified Information Systems Security Professional (CISSP), or similar credentials are preferred. Candidates should also demonstrate excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills and a commitment to working effectively with diverse student populations. Indiana Tech is a student-centered institution dedicated to providing career-focused education that prepares graduates to thrive in a technology-driven global economy. Located in Fort Wayne, Indiana, the university is recognized for its commitment to innovation, applied learning, industry partnerships, and student success. Faculty enjoy the opportunity to work in a collaborative academic environment while helping shape the future of computing, cybersecurity, artificial intelligence, and engineering education. **Application materials must include Vita and unofficial transcripts. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
