    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/9B7DD7DDF4B46DE388E0D590C86BBE1D/jobs/266622": {
      "title": "Spirit Director",
      "description": "Spirit Director You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Spirit Director Hot Job Fort Wayne Campus - Fort Wayne, IN 46803 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level Bachelor's Category Athletics Apply Description Indiana Tech is a thriving, independent, teaching-oriented university that delivers career-oriented programming in a wide variety of disciplines that includes business, engineering, computer sciences, criminal justice, cybersecurity, marketing, health sciences, communication and helping professions. Indiana Tech enrolls nearly 1,500 students in its traditional undergraduate programs on its picturesque main campus, and nearly 5,000 students in its adult and online program. We offer degrees at the associate, bachelor’s, master's, and doctoral levels and undergraduate and graduate certificates. Over 41% of our students are either globally or domestically diverse; this contributes to our unique vibrant and inclusive campus community. All academic programs are designed to provide students with relevant and practical experiences, including an emphasis on internships. The university is accredited by the Higher Learning Commission. Indiana Tech is committed to fostering a welcoming and respectful environment for all. We actively support the recruitment, engagement, and retention of students, faculty, and staff from a wide range of experiences, backgrounds, and perspectives. We believe that creating a sense of connection and support across our campus community plays an essential role in preparing students to succeed and contribute in a global society. Indiana Tech has big plans for its future. Learn more at Indiana Tech Strategic Plan or strategicplan.indianatech.edu . General Summary The Indiana Tech Warrior Athletics team is seeking an energetic and student-focused professional to lead our cheer, dance, and band programs. The Department of Athletics at Indiana Tech serves as an integral part of the university and is an important participant in its mission. The commitment of the Department of Athletics is to enhance the student experience and to provide quality programs that are competitive, fun, and meaningful in an atmosphere that promotes success within the spirit of fair play, sportsmanship, and integrity. Essential Duties & Responsibilities Plan, develop, and administer all aspects of the cheer, dance and band programs Apparel, scheduling, travel, etc. Formulate and administer team policies aligning with the philosophy of the institution Select, supervise, and mentor assistant coaches for the program Recruit and retain specific enrollment numbers yearly Prepare students to meet eligibility qualifications for NAIA, WHAC and Indiana Tech or other outside affiliates Support the mission, vision, and strategic plan of Indiana Tech Prepare a budget for review by the Athletic Director Purchase needed equipment and supplies necessary with the approval of the Athletic Director Document and report all scores to the appropriate outlets Prepare, maintain, and schedule facilities for practices, games, and meetings Provide a written evaluation of the program at the conclusion of each season Complete other duties as assigned by the Athletic Department or University Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; master’s degree preferred. Experience 1-3 years of college playing or coaching experience preferred Working Conditions Physical work and travel are required. Work is performed during traditional and non-traditional hours. Night and weekend work is common, during specific time periods. Application materials must include a cover letter and resume. Applicants must be prepared to provide a written response to Tech's mission and vision. The position remains open until filled; a review of candidates will commence as application materials are received. Share job details to About Indiana Tech Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
